TOF-27 SplitTryte CPU Instruction & Architecture Mappings v1.0

Direct instruction set opcodes with corresponding mappings to popular CPU architectures (x86_64, ARM64, and Raspberry Pi / Broadcom).

[LAYOUT]
splitTryte = [11|OPTIONS|BANK_L|VAL_L2|VAL_L1|VAL_L0|BANK_R|VAL_R2|VAL_R1|VAL_R0]
standard_marker = 11

[DESIGN_RULES]

1. Every splitTryte stores two self-contained instruction opcodes.
2. Columns represent target assembly equivalents for popular architectures: x86_64, ARM64, and Raspberry Pi (BCM2835/ARMv7+ or VideoCore GPU asm).
3. BANK:+ is Control Flow & System Operations.
4. BANK:- is Memory & Data Movement.
5. BANK:0 is Arithmetic & Logic.
6. Full pair table is generated by crossing every left opcode against every right opcode.

[BANK_LANES]

+ = UPPER_ALPHA          = 10
- = LOWER_ALPHA          = 00
0 = NETIV_NUMERIC_SYMBOL = 01

[VAL_LANES]
00 = --- = 00|00|00
01 = --0 = 00|00|01
02 = --+ = 00|00|10
03 = -0- = 00|01|00
04 = -00 = 00|01|01
05 = -0+ = 00|01|10
06 = -+- = 00|10|00
07 = -+0 = 00|10|01
08 = -++ = 00|10|10
09 = 0-- = 01|00|00
10 = 0-0 = 01|00|01
11 = 0-+ = 01|00|10
12 = 00- = 01|01|00
13 = 000 = 01|01|01
14 = 00+ = 01|01|10
15 = 0+- = 01|10|00
16 = 0+0 = 01|10|01
17 = 0++ = 01|10|10
18 = +-- = 10|00|00
19 = +-0 = 10|00|01
20 = +-+ = 10|00|10
21 = +0- = 10|01|00
22 = +00 = 10|01|01
23 = +0+ = 10|01|10
24 = ++- = 10|10|00
25 = ++0 = 10|10|01
26 = +++ = 10|10|10

[BANK:+] CONTROL_FLOW_AND_SYSTEM
00 --- 00|00|00 NOP   | nop                 | nop               | nop                  | No Operation
01 --0 00|00|01 HLT   | hlt                 | wfi               | wfi                  | Halt / Wait For Interrupt
02 --+ 00|00|10 JMP   | jmp addr            | b addr            | b addr               | Unconditional branch
03 -0- 00|01|00 CALL  | call addr           | bl addr           | bl addr              | Call subroutine
04 -00 00|01|01 RET   | ret                 | ret               | ret                  | Return from subroutine
05 -0+ 00|01|10 CMP   | cmp reg, reg        | cmp reg, reg      | cmp reg, reg         | Compare values
06 -+- 00|10|00 TST   | test reg, reg       | tst reg, reg      | tst reg, reg         | Test bit mask
07 -+0 00|10|01 JEQ   | je addr             | b.eq addr         | b.eq addr            | Branch if Equal
08 -++ 00|10|10 JNE   | jne addr            | b.ne addr         | b.ne addr            | Branch if Not Equal
09 0-- 01|00|00 JLT   | jl addr             | b.lt addr         | b.lt addr            | Branch if Less Than
10 0-0 01|00|01 JGT   | jg addr             | b.gt addr         | b.gt addr            | Branch if Greater Than
11 0-+ 01|00|10 JLE   | jle addr            | b.le addr         | b.le addr            | Branch if Less or Equal
12 00- 01|01|00 JGE   | jge addr            | b.ge addr         | b.ge addr            | Branch if Greater or Equal
13 000 01|01|01 SYS   | syscall             | svc #0            | svc #0               | System call / Supervisor Call
14 00+ 01|01|10 INT   | int imm             | svc imm           | svc imm              | Software interrupt
15 0+- 01|10|00 IRET  | iret                | eret              | eret                 | Interrupt return
16 0+0 01|10|01 CLI   | cli                 | msr daifset, #2   | cpsid i              | Disable Interrupts
17 0++ 01|10|10 STI   | sti                 | msr daifclr, #2   | cpsie i              | Enable Interrupts
18 +-- 10|00|00 IN    | in al, dx           | ldr al, [dx]      | ldr al, [dx]         | Input from port / MMIO
19 +-0 10|00|01 OUT   | out dx, al          | str al, [dx]      | str al, [dx]         | Output to port / MMIO
20 +-+ 10|00|10 BRK   | int3                | brk #0            | bkpt #0              | Software breakpoint
21 +0- 10|01|00 LIDT  | lidt mem            | msr vbar_el1, reg | msr vbar_el1, reg    | Load Interrupt Vector Table
22 +00 10|01|01 TLB   | invlpg mem          | tlbi vmalle1      | tlbi vmalle1         | Invalidate TLB Entry
23 +0+ 10|01|10 WBINV | wbinvd              | dc civac, reg     | dc civac, reg        | Cache Writeback & Invalidate
24 ++- 10|10|00 CPUID | cpuid               | mrs reg, midr_el1 | mrs reg, midr_el1    | Query CPU Identification
25 ++0 10|10|01 YIELD | pause               | yield             | yield                | Yield thread slice
26 +++ 10|10|10 FENCE | mfence              | dmb sy            | dmb sy               | Memory barrier/fence

[BANK:-] MEMORY_AND_DATA_MOVEMENT
00 --- 00|00|00 MOV   | mov dst, src        | mov dst, src      | mov dst, src         | Move reg/imm to reg
01 --0 00|00|01 LDR   | mov reg, [mem]      | ldr reg, [mem]    | ldr reg, [mem]       | Load from Memory
02 --+ 00|00|10 STR   | mov [mem], reg      | str reg, [mem]    | str reg, [mem]       | Store to Memory
03 -0- 00|01|00 LDP   | movups              | ldp reg1, reg2    | ldp reg1, reg2       | Load Pair of Registers
04 -00 00|01|01 STP   | movups              | stp reg1, reg2    | stp reg1, reg2       | Store Pair of Registers
05 -0+ 00|01|10 PUSH  | push reg            | str reg, [sp,-16]!| push {reg}           | Push onto Stack
06 -+- 00|10|00 POP   | pop reg             | ldr reg, [sp], 16 | pop {reg}            | Pop from Stack
07 -+0 00|10|01 LEA   | lea reg, [mem]      | adrp/add reg, mem | adr/add reg, mem     | Load Effective Address
08 -++ 00|10|10 MOVZX | movzx dst, src      | uxtw dst, src     | uxtw dst, src        | Move with Zero Extend
09 0-- 01|00|00 MOVSX | movsx dst, src      | sxtw dst, src     | sxtw dst, src        | Move with Sign Extend
10 0-0 01|00|01 XCHG  | xchg reg, reg       | swp reg, reg      | swp reg, reg         | Exchange register values
11 0-+ 01|00|10 CMPXCH| cmpxchg dst, src    | cas dst, src      | cas dst, src         | Compare & Exchange (Atomic)
12 00- 01|01|00 LDAR  | mov + mfence        | ldar reg, [mem]   | ldar reg, [mem]      | Load Acquire (Atomic)
13 000 01|01|01 STLR  | mov + mfence        | stlr reg, [mem]   | stlr reg, [mem]      | Store Release (Atomic)
14 00+ 01|01|10 PREF  | prefetcht0 [mem]    | prfm pldl1keep    | prfm pldl1keep       | Prefetch Cache Line
15 0+- 01|10|00 CLFL  | clflush [mem]       | dc cvac, reg      | dc cvac, reg         | Flush Cache Line
16 0+0 01|10|01 MEMCPY| rep movsb           | memcpy            | memcpy               | Copy block of memory
17 0++ 01|10|10 MEMSET| rep stosb           | memset            | memset               | Fill block of memory
18 +-- 10|00|00 ALLOCA| sub rsp, reg        | sub sp, reg       | sub sp, reg          | Allocate stack frame
19 +-0 10|00|01 SWP   | xchg                | swp               | swp                  | Atomic register/memory swap
20 +-+ 10|00|10 LL    | mov                 | ldxr              | ldrex                | Load Link / Load Exclusive
21 +0- 10|01|00 SC    | cmpxchg             | stxr              | strex                | Store Conditional / Exclusive
22 +00 10|01|01 MSR   | wrmsr               | msr sysreg, reg   | msr sysreg, reg      | Write System Register
23 +0+ 10|01|10 MRS   | rdmsr               | mrs reg, sysreg   | mrs reg, sysreg      | Read System Register
24 ++- 10|10|00 INVL  | invlpg              | tlbi              | tlbi                 | Invalidate Cache Page
25 ++0 10|10|01 SETCR | mov cr0, reg        | msr sctlr_el1, reg| msr sctlr_el1, reg   | Write Control Register
26 +++ 10|10|10 GETCR | mov reg, cr0        | mrs reg, sctlr_el1| mrs reg, sctlr_el1   | Read Control Register

[BANK:0] ARITHMETIC_AND_LOGIC
00 --- 00|00|00 ADD   | add dst, src        | add dst, src1, s2 | add dst, src1, s2    | Add values
01 --0 00|00|01 SUB   | sub dst, src        | sub dst, src1, s2 | sub dst, src1, s2    | Subtract values
02 --+ 00|00|10 MUL   | imul dst, src       | mul dst, src1, s2 | mul dst, src1, s2    | Multiply values
03 -0- 00|01|00 DIV   | idiv src            | sdiv dst, src1, s2| sdiv dst, src1, s2   | Divide values
04 -00 00|01|01 ADC   | adc dst, src        | adc dst, src1, s2 | adc dst, src1, s2    | Add with carry flag
05 -0+ 00|01|10 SBB   | sbb dst, src        | sbc dst, src1, s2 | sbc dst, src1, s2    | Subtract with borrow flag
06 -+- 00|10|00 INC   | inc reg             | add reg, reg, #1  | add reg, reg, #1     | Increment value by 1
07 -+0 00|10|01 DEC   | dec reg             | sub reg, reg, #1  | sub reg, reg, #1     | Decrement value by 1
08 -++ 00|10|10 NEG   | neg reg             | neg reg, reg      | neg reg, reg         | Two's complement negate
09 0-- 01|00|00 AND   | and dst, src        | and dst, src1, s2 | and dst, src1, s2    | Bitwise AND
10 0-0 01|00|01 ORR   | or dst, src         | orr dst, src1, s2 | orr dst, src1, s2    | Bitwise OR
11 0-+ 01|00|10 XOR   | xor dst, src        | eor dst, src1, s2 | eor dst, src1, s2    | Bitwise Exclusive OR
12 00- 01|01|00 NOT   | not reg             | mvn reg, reg      | mvn reg, reg         | Bitwise NOT (invert)
13 000 01|01|01 SHL   | shl reg, imm        | lsl reg, reg, imm | lsl reg, reg, imm    | Logical shift left
14 00+ 01|01|10 SHR   | shr reg, imm        | lsr reg, reg, imm | lsr reg, reg, imm    | Logical shift right
15 0+- 01|10|00 SAR   | sar reg, imm        | asr reg, reg, imm | asr reg, reg, imm    | Arithmetic shift right
16 0+0 01|10|01 ROL   | rol reg, imm        | ror reg, reg, imm | ror reg, reg, imm    | Rotate left (emulated)
17 0++ 01|10|10 ROR   | ror reg, imm        | ror reg, reg, imm | ror reg, reg, imm    | Rotate right
18 +-- 10|00|00 MADD  | imul + add          | madd dst, s1,s2,s3| madd dst, s1,s2,s3   | Multiply-accumulate
19 +-0 10|00|01 MSUB  | imul - sub          | msub dst, s1,s2,s3| msub dst, s1,s2,s3   | Multiply-subtract
20 +-+ 10|00|10 BSWAP | bswap reg           | rev reg, reg      | rev reg, reg         | Swap byte order
21 +0- 10|01|00 CLZ   | bsr + xor           | clz reg, reg      | clz reg, reg         | Count leading zeros
22 +00 10|01|01 CTZ   | tzcnt               | rbit + clz        | rbit + clz           | Count trailing zeros
23 +0+ 10|01|10 POPCNT| popcnt dst, src     | cnt reg           | cnt reg              | Population count of bits
24 ++- 10|10|00 ADDS  | add + jo            | adds dst, s1, s2  | adds dst, s1, s2     | Add and set status flags
25 ++0 10|10|01 SUBS  | sub + jo            | subs dst, s1, s2  | subs dst, s1, s2     | Subtract & set status flags
26 +++ 10|10|10 ASR   | sar                 | asr               | asr                  | Arithmetic shift right (reg)

[PAIR_TABLE_RULE]
For every left symbol L in all banks and every right symbol R in all banks:

pair_id = left_global_index * 81 + right_global_index

splitTryte_lanes = [11|OPTIONS|BANK_L_BITS|VAL_L_BITS|BANK_R_BITS|VAL_R_BITS]

Global bank order:
0..26   = BANK:+
27..53  = BANK:-
54..80  = BANK:0

[PAIR_ID_LAYOUT]
left_global_index  = pair_id / 81
right_global_index = pair_id % 81

global_symbol_index:
00..26 = BANK:+ values 00..26
27..53 = BANK:- values 00..26
54..80 = BANK:0 values 00..26

[EXAMPLES]
ADD MOV = 000 +00 = [11|00|01|00|00|00|00|00|00|00] (Left: BANK:0 VAL:00, Right: BANK:- VAL:00)

[COUNTS]
banks = 3
symbols_per_bank = 27
total_symbols = 81
splitTryte_pair_slots = 81 * 81 = 6561